{"name":"Vermilion Seabass","hex":"#973a36","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vermilion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vivid red synthetic pigment made of mercury sulfide, cinnabar.","A bright orange-red colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brilliant red colour.","Having the color of the vermilion dye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vermilion"},{"term":"seabass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of sea bass, used especially in compound terms."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seabass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coral grouper","blocks":[{"text":"Cephalopholis miniata, commonly known as the coral grouper, coral hind, coral rock cod, coral cod, coral trout, round-tailed trout or vermillion seabass is a species of marine ray-finned fish, a grouper of the family Epinephelidae. It is associated with coral reefs and occurs in the Indo-Pacific."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Coral_grouper_%28Cephalopholis_miniata%29_-_49878455087.jpg/330px-Coral_grouper_%28Cephalopholis_miniata%29_-_49878455087.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_grouper"},{"title":"Vermilion","blocks":[{"text":"Vermilion is a color family and toxic pigment most often used between antiquity and the 19th century and made from the powdered mineral cinnabar. It is synonymous with red orange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Lacquerware-roundbox-w-children.jpg/330px-Lacquerware-roundbox-w-children.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vermilion"},{"title":"Sea bass","blocks":[{"text":"Sea bass is a common name for a variety of species of marine fish. Many fish species of various families have been called sea bass. For the purpose of this article, sea bass and seabass ar